    "b-impk-d1": {
      "id": "b-impk-d1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": storage/ddl.ts is the schema of record and migrations are ordered and validated against the applied bookkeeping at open; the drizzle mirror in storage/schema.ts is a typed convenience and may lag. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": a hand-written DDL with CHECK constraints (XOR subjects, digest-with-code, one live fact per subject and type) carries invariants the ORM cannot express. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": every future table or index: add it to the DDL and a numbered migration first."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-impk-d2": {
      "id": "b-impk-d2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": apply is the only module that writes fact, evidence, link, or curated entity rows, and it takes a proposal envelope, never an open handle to the model. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": one validator, one place for scope, citation, and overwrite rules; the legacy system had several. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": librarian, backfill, and any future knowledge writer."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-impk-d3": {
      "id": "b-impk-d3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the index database is derived and disposable; nothing reads it as truth and every build is a full replacement per table. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": search quality changes with chunking and models; a rebuild must be free. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": index/*."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-impk-d4": {
      "id": "b-impk-d4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": knowledge jobs are CLIs inside their owning module, dispatched by the application job runner as kg2-*. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the dispatcher stays a routing table and each job's flags live beside the code they drive. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": every future knowledge job."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-impk-d5": {
      "id": "b-impk-d5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the legacy slice keeps only what still has readers: the code graph and its builders (worker and librarian graph tools, kg-* jobs), the learnings ledger (ledger_search, the summarizer's transcript loader, the dashboard route), and standards. Nothing new is added there. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the worker profile has not moved yet; deleting the graph would take four worker tools with it. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": apps/server/src/core/knowledge; its exit is tracked in the knowledge worklist."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
